cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "AxiSim: GPU-accelerated axisymmetric CFD solver"
message: "If you use this software, please cite the archived release below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Tsumura
    given-names: Lui
    email: luitsumura@gmail.com
repository-code: "https://github.com/Luippe/AxiSim-Software"
url: "https://github.com/Luippe/AxiSim-Software"
abstract: >-
  AxiSim is an interactive finite-volume solver for axisymmetric incompressible
  flow. It solves the incompressible Navier-Stokes equations in axisymmetric
  (r-z) coordinates using the SIMPLE pressure-velocity coupling scheme, with the
  linear algebra running on the GPU through CUDA. Geometry sketching, meshing,
  solving, and post-processing are combined in a single real-time interface,
  with optional energy and concentration scalar transport.
keywords:
  - computational fluid dynamics
  - axisymmetric flow
  - finite volume method
  - Navier-Stokes
  - SIMPLE algorithm
  - CUDA
  - GPU computing
